### Key observations

**Two mandated caps did all the damage.** Uncapped, this profile scores E8/O8 and lands at 8.4 — right on the Matt-Smith anchor. Both caps are load-bearing and both are verified against the text, not inferred.

**Evidence capped at 6 — and the script gave a false PASS.** `blog-source-audit.mjs` reports 5/5 inline, 0 untagged. It's wrong here: its slot detection returned "(no quoted material in slot)" for both EMPATHY TURN and CLOSE, and it never scans the childhood section or the rabbit hole. By hand there are ~16 untagged quotes, including the empathy turn's entire pivot ("*I don't know if I would be able to be as confident to speak out on other things if I felt that my whole life was up for grabs*" — no outlet, no date) and the quote the draft itself introduces as "the line that carries the rest of his life." The body also has zero outbound hyperlinks against ~15 outlets named in prose. **This is worth fixing in the audit script, not just this draft** — that slot-detection gap will keep passing drafts with unsourced empathy turns.

**Originality capped at 7 — six house moves reused** against Prince-Harry, Ms-Rachel (08-20) and Bill-Burr (08-19). The TL;DR is near-verbatim Bill-Burr's skeleton (six bullets, bold-noun-phrase-colon), the final "what the type misses" bullet is Ms-Rachel's, and the aphoristic section-closer cadence was flagged by this draft's own fresh-eyes review (seven in a row) with exactly one removed. Note the automated `same-type-similarity.mjs` scan came back **clear** (top pair 0.058, noise floor) — it only reads diagnosis/counter-typing slots, so it can't see furniture reuse.

**What's genuinely excellent and should survive revision:** the diagnosis section argues with a control condition — it discounts two of its own three exhibits because "being closeted does most of that work on anybody, whatever their type," then rests the call on the backflip at thirty-seven where nobody was reading him. The Richard II section concedes real critic pressure before answering it with a mechanism. The 1p handling — flagging that his campaigning figure has no published source, producing the one that does (LGBT+ Consortium, March 2025), then refusing to call it a refutation — is better than most published journalism. Discoverability is near the corpus ceiling.

**One stale ledger:** the FORMULA FINGERPRINT block still names the empathy-turn section "Why Jonathan Bailey Will Not Say Who He Is Dating," a heading the editor pass retitled away.

